{"openapi":"3.1.1","info":{"title":"Intelliprint API Reference","description":"Send mail as easily as sending email. With the Intelliprint API, you can send letters and postcards in just a few lines of code.\n\nThe API is designed to be [REST-ful](https://w.wiki/4YH8). Every resource has a predictable URL, and every endpoint accepts data encoded as [JSON](https://w.wiki/Qi$) or [multipart/form-data](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7578). Responses are JSON-encoded with standard HTTP status codes.\n\nAuthentication requires an API key ([create one here](https://account.intelliprint.net/api_keys)) in the `Authorization` header.\n\nQuestions or feedback? We're here to help at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net).","version":"1.0.0","contact":{"name":"Intelliprint Support","email":"hello@intelliprint.net","url":"https://intelliprint.net"},"termsOfService":"https://intelliprint.net/terms","license":{"name":"MIT","identifier":"MIT"},"x-scalar-sdk-installation":[{"lang":"JavaScript","description":"Install our **Node.js SDK** from npm:","source":"npm install intelliprint"},{"lang":"Node","description":"Install our **Node.js SDK** from npm:","source":"npm install intelliprint"},{"lang":"custom","description":"Install our **Node.js SDK** from npm:","source":"npm install intelliprint"}]},"servers":[{"url":"https://api.intelliprint.net/v1","description":"Base URL"}],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"tags":[{"name":"Prints","description":"Print jobs are the core resource in the Intelliprint API. Each print job represents a collection of letters or postcards to be sent.\n\nPrint jobs are completely flexible. A single print job can contain one letter or postcard, or thousands at once. For programmatic use cases, __you can send thousands of mail items with just one API call__. For human-driven workflows, you can create a draft, preview it, make edits, and confirm it for printing when ready.\n\n> [!note] \n> While you're testing, use the `testmode` parameter. When set to `true`, your account is not charged and mail is not actually sent."},{"name":"Backgrounds","description":"Backgrounds allow you to apply reusable designs and artwork to your print jobs. Use them for letterheads, logos, and other recurring design elements."},{"name":"Mailing Lists","description":"Mailinxg lists store groups of recipients, allowing you to send mail to multiple people with a single operation."},{"name":"Mailing List Recipients","description":"Mailing list recipients represent the individual contacts stored within a mailing list. Manage recipients to control who receives your mail campaigns."}],"externalDocs":{"description":"Quickstart guide and examples","url":"https://docs.intelliprint.net"},"components":{"securitySchemes":{"BearerAuth":{"type":"http","scheme":"bearer","bearerFormat":"API key","description":"Provide your account's API key. [Create one here](https://account.intelliprint.net/api_keys)."}},"schemas":{"ErrorObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"message":{"type":"string","description":"A human-readable message describing the error. You can display this to your users to help them understand what went wrong.","examples":["Received unknown parameter: testmood (Did you mean testmode?)"]},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The general category of the error.","enum":["invalid_request_error","authentication_error","payment_error","rate_limited","internal_error"],"examples":["invalid_request_error"]},"code":{"type":"string","description":"A unique code for the specific error that occurred.","enum":["parameter_invalid","parameter_missing","parameter_unknown","body_too_large","body_incorrect_format","no_api_key","invalid_api_key","logged_out","forbidden","payment_error","not_found","rate_limited","refused","internal_error"],"examples":["parameter_unknown"]},"param":{"type":"string","description":"The parameter that caused the error, if applicable.","examples":["testmood"]}}}}},"PrintObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for the print job.","examples":["print_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `print`.","const":"print"},"testmode":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the print job is in test mode. When enabled, your account is not charged and mail is not sent.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"account":{"type":"string","description":"The Intelliprint account ID that the print job belongs to.","examples":["acc_eg"]},"user":{"type":["object","null"],"description":"The user who initiated the print job. This value is `null` for API-initiated print jobs.","examples":[null,{"id":"user_eg","object":"user","name":"John Doe","email":"john.doe@example.com","phone":"+1234567890","profile_picture":"https://cdn.storage.com/intelliprint/users/user_ID.jpg","password":false,"mfa":{"enabled":true},"tos_agreed":true,"disable_notifications":false,"created":1761955200}]},"team":{"type":["object","null"],"description":"The team associated with the print job. This value is `null` for API-initiated print jobs.","examples":[null,{"id":"team_eg","object":"team","account":"acc_eg","name":"Marketing Team","default":{},"created":1761955200}]},"reference":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly description of this print job. This value is displayed in the dashboard for easier identification.","examples":["Marketing pamphlet for J. Doe"]},"confirmed":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the print job has been confirmed. Once confirmed, the print job is submitted for printing and cannot be updated. You can confirm a print job in the dashboard or by setting the `confirmed` parameter via the API.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of mailings present in the print job.","enum":["letter","postcard"],"default":"letter"},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The total number of pages across all mailings in the print job. This may be the same as or more than `sheets` if double-sided printing is used.","examples":[10]},"sheets":{"type":"integer","description":"The total number of physical sheets across all mailings in the print job. Sheets are the physical paper that pages are printed on.","examples":[5]},"file":{"type":"object","description":"Details about the file uploaded to create the print job.","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the file uploaded when creating the print job. This also serves as the default `reference` if one is not provided.","examples":["eg_file.pdf"]},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages in the uploaded file.","examples":[10]},"size":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The size of the file uploaded in bytes.","examples":[1024000]}}},"splitting":{"type":"object","description":"Splitting settings for the print job. Used when a single file contains multiple letters with pre-inserted addresses. Splitting is only available for letters.","properties":{"method":{"type":"string","description":"The method used to split the print job into mailings.","enum":["none","split_on_phrase","split_on_pages","mailing_list"],"default":"none"},"phrase":{"type":"string","description":"The phrase to search for on each page to split the print job into multiple letters. Only used when method is `split_on_phrase`. The phrase should appear once on the first page of each letter. Tip: Use white text to hide the phrase from recipients.","examples":["Dear"]},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages each letter in a split print job should have. Only used if method is `split_on_pages`.","examples":[1]}}},"printing":{"type":"object","description":"Printing settings for the print job, including quality, color, single or double-sided printing, and finishing options. Single-sided printing is the default.","properties":{"double_sided":{"type":"string","description":"Whether this print job should be printed on both sides of the paper.\n\nIf you choose `mixed`, you need to specify the page indexes to print double sided in the `double_sided_specific_pages` property.\n\nThis is only available for letters.","enum":["no","yes","mixed"],"default":"no"},"double_sided_specific_pages":{"type":"array","description":"The page indexes to print double-sided. Only used if `double_sided` is `mixed`. This is only available for letters. Page indexes are 0-indexed (first page is index 0).","items":{"type":"integer","description":"The page index to print double-sided.","examples":[0,1,2]}},"premium_quality":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in premium quality. Premium quality is optional for letters, while postcards are always printed in premium quality due to their glossy finish.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"black_and_white":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in black and white instead of color. This is only available for letters.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"matt_finish":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed with a matt finish. This is only available for postcards as letters are always printed on matt paper.","examples":[true,false],"default":false}}},"postage":{"type":"object","description":"Postage settings for the print job, including the postage service, ideal envelope (or postcard size), and mailing date.","properties":{"service":{"type":"string","description":"The postage service to use for the print job. Postcards can currently only be sent with `uk_second_class` or `uk_first_class` services.","enum":["uk_second_class","uk_second_class_signed_for","uk_first_class","uk_first_class_signed_for","uk_special_delivery_9am","uk_special_delivery","international","tracked_24","tracked_48"],"default":"uk_second_class"},"ideal_envelope":{"type":"string","description":"The ideal envelope size for letters or postcard size for postcards.\n\nAvailable values are `c4`, `c5`, `c4_plus`, `a4_box` for letters, and `postcard_a6`, `postcard_a5` or `postcard_a5_enveloped` for postcards. Default is `c5` for letters and `postcard_a6` for postcards.\n\nThe API may upgrade a letter to a larger envelope if the content is too large for the chosen envelope size.","enum":["c4","c5","c4_plus","a4_box","postcard_a6","postcard_a5","postcard_a5_enveloped"],"default":"c5"},"mail_date":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The mailing date for the print job. This is when we will print and ship your mailing, not when it will arrive at the recipient's address. This is a [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) (day-adjusted). Use this field to schedule mailings for a future date.","examples":[1761955200]}}},"background":{"type":"object","description":"Background settings for the print job. Specify which backgrounds to apply to different pages. This is only available for letters.","properties":{"first_page":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the first page of the print job. Typically a letterhead or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]},"other_pages":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the other pages of the print job. Typically a continuation design or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]}}},"confidential":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be considered confidential. Confidential print jobs cannot be viewed by other users in the dashboard.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"extra_documents":{"type":"array","description":"Extra documents (or additional documents) can be sent alongside letters in the print job. These can include standard terms and conditions, brochures, forms, or other supplementary materials.\n\nA copy of all extra documents is sent with each letter in the print job.\n\nExtra documents are only available for letters, as postcards have a fixed size.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for the extra document uploaded.","examples":["extra_eg"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The filename of the uploaded document.","examples":["eg_file.pdf"]},"apply_background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to apply the `background.other_pages` to the extra document. Default is false.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages in the extra document.","examples":[10]},"size":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The size of the extra document in bytes.","examples":[1024000]}}}},"remove_letters":{"type":"object","description":"Used alongside the `splitting` settings to remove specific letters from the print job.","properties":{"with_phrase":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"If this phrase is present in a letter, it will be removed from the print job. This is only available for letters.","examples":["EMAIL ONLY"]}}},"nudge":{"type":"object","description":"For print jobs with pre-inserted addresses, nudging helps position the address within the envelope window. Nudging is only available for letters.","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","description":"The horizontal distance to nudge the address window to the right in millimeters.","examples":[2]},"y":{"type":"number","description":"The vertical distance to nudge the address window down in millimeters.","examples":[-1]}}},"letters":{"type":"array","description":"An array of letters or postcards present in the print job.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for this mail item.","examples":["letter_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `letter` for both letters and postcards.","const":"letter"},"status":{"type":"string","description":"The status of the mail item, representing its lifecycle from creation to dispatch.","enum":["draft","waiting_to_print","printing","enclosing","shipping","sent","cancelled","returned","failed_wrong_address"],"default":"draft"},"postage_service":{"type":"string","description":"The postage service used to ship the mail item.","enum":["uk_second_class","uk_second_class_signed_for","uk_first_class","uk_first_class_signed_for","uk_special_delivery_9am","uk_special_delivery","international","tracked_24","tracked_48"],"default":"uk_second_class"},"tracking_number":{"type":"string","description":"The Royal Mail tracking number of the mail item.\n\nThis is only available for tracked shipping services, `uk_second_class_signed_for`, `uk_first_class_signed_for`, `uk_special_delivery_9am`, `uk_special_delivery`, `tracked_24` or `tracked_48`.","examples":["1234567890"]},"shipped_date":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the mail item was shipped out. We use UNIX timestamps to mitigate any timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]},"returned":{"type":"object","description":"Details concerning why a mail item was returned.\n\nThis object is only present if the mail item has a status of `returned`.","properties":{"acknowledged":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the mail item's return has been acknowledged on the dashboard.","examples":[true,false]},"date":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the mail item was returned to us. We use UNIX timestamps to mitigate any timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"A free-form reason why the mail item was returned.","examples":["Not at this address","Delivery Refused","Incorrect Address"]}}},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages in the mail item. Pages might be the same as, or more than `sheets` if double-sided printing is chosen.","examples":[10]},"sheets":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of sheets in the mail item. Sheets are the physical paper sheets that pages are printed on.","examples":[5]},"envelope":{"type":"string","description":"The exact envelope a letter will be enclosed in or the postcard size.","enum":["c4","c5","c4_plus","a4_box","postcard_a6","postcard_a5","postcard_a5_enveloped"],"default":"c5"},"address_window":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The position of the address window on the envelope. This is only available for letters.","enum":["left","right"],"default":"left"},"add_address_sheet":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the address is printed on a separate page followed by your letter (If `true`) or if the address is printed on the same page as your letter (If `false`).","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"address":{"type":"object","description":"The address the mail item is being sent to.","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The address line.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postcode of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country of the address.","examples":["GB"],"default":"GB"}}},"cost":{"type":"object","description":"The pricing details for the individual mail item.","properties":{"amount":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"This is the basic pre-tax cost of the individual mail item.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[100000000]},"tax":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"This is the tax amount applicable to the basic cost of the individual mail item.\n\nWe only charge VAT for our customers in the United Kingdom. Customers in other countries will see a tax amount of 0.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[20000000]},"after_tax":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The total cost of the individual mail item after tax.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[120000000]},"currency":{"type":"string","description":"This is the 3-letter currency code of the cost. This is an [ISO 4217 currency code](https://www.iban.com/currency-codes). Example: `GBP`. We currently only present costs in `GBP`.","examples":["GBP"],"default":"GBP"}}},"weight":{"type":"number","description":"The calculated weight of the mail item in grams.","examples":[28]},"print_stream":{"type":"string","description":"This is primarily an internal field which describes the printer tray the mail item will be sent to for printing and enclosing.","examples":["uk_second_class-c5-standard"]},"pdf_status":{"type":"string","description":"This field describes whether the underlying PDF for a mail item has been deleted or not.","enum":["built","deleted"],"default":"built"},"pdf":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"uri","description":"A URL to a PDF preview of the mail item. This is a signed URL that will expire after 1 hour. This will be `null` if the `pdf_status` is `deleted`.","examples":["https://cdn.storage.com/intelliprint/letters/letter_ID.pdf",null]},"passthrough_exported":{"type":["boolean","null"],"description":"This is primarily an internal field. For certain shipping services, we register mail items with them and keep track of it in this field.","examples":[true,false,null],"default":false}}}},"cost":{"type":"object","description":"The pricing details for the entire print job.","properties":{"amount":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"This is the basic pre-tax cost of the print job.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[100000000]},"tax":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"This is the tax amount applicable to the basic cost of the print job.\n\nWe only charge VAT for our customers in the United Kingdom. Customers in other countries will see a tax amount of 0.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[20000000]},"after_tax":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The total cost of the print job after tax. This is the amount charged to you for submitting this print job.\n\n__All costs amounts returned by the API need to be divided by 10^8 (100000000) to get the real `GBP` price.__ We factor in 8 decimal places for sub-penny precision of large bulk orders.","examples":[120000000]},"currency":{"type":"string","description":"This is the 3-letter currency code of the cost. This is an [ISO 4217 currency code](https://www.iban.com/currency-codes). Example: `GBP`. We currently only present costs in `GBP`.","examples":["GBP"],"default":"GBP"}}},"confirmation_email":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether a confirmation email should be sent to the account owner once the print job is confirmed.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"insert":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"This property is not present in the response if an insert ID is not provided while creating or updating a print job. Inserts are a value-added service - We can keep stock of and insert any pre-printed materials provided ahead of time into envelopes for you. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","examples":["ins_eg"]},"template":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the template used to create this print job.","examples":["tmpl_eg"]},"mailing_list":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the mailing list used to create this print job.","examples":["mal_eg"]},"address_window":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The position of the address window on the envelope. This is only available for letters.","enum":["left","right"],"default":"left"},"confirmed_at":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the print job was confirmed. We use UNIX timestamps to mitigate any timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]},"created":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the print job was created. We use UNIX timestamps to mitigate any timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]},"metadata":{"type":"object","description":"This is an arbitrary object that can be used to store any additional data alongside your print job. This is not used by Intelliprint and is only for your own use.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"uploaded_by":"J. Doe","internal_id":"123456"}]}}},"ListObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `list`.","const":"list"},"data":{"type":"array","description":"An array of objects returned by the API.","items":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BackgroundObject"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListObject"},{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListRecipientObject"}]}},"total_available":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The total number of objects available that can be returned by the API using successive paginated requests.","examples":[100]},"has_more":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether there are more objects available that can be requested in the next paginated request.","examples":[true]}}},"BackgroundObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for the background.","examples":["bg_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `background`.","const":"background"},"account":{"type":"string","description":"The Intelliprint account ID that the background belongs to.","examples":["acc_eg"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this background. This name is used for the selection menu in the dashboard print editor.","examples":["Company Letterhead"]},"file":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the file uploaded as the background.","examples":["eg_file.pdf"]},"size":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The size of the file uploaded as the background in bytes.","examples":[1024000]}}},"team":{"type":["object","null"],"description":"The team that the background is available to. Can be set to `null` to make the background available to everyone.","examples":[null,{"id":"team_eg","object":"team","account":"acc_eg","name":"Marketing Team","default":{},"created":1761955200}]},"pdf":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"uri","description":"A URL to a PDF example of the background. This is a signed URL that will expire after 1 hour.","examples":["https://cdn.storage.com/intelliprint/backgrounds/bg_ID.pdf"]},"created":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the background was created. We use UNIX timestamps to avoid timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]}}},"MailingListObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for the mailing list.","examples":["mal_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `mailing_list`.","const":"mailing_list"},"account":{"type":"string","description":"The Intelliprint account ID that the mailing list belongs to.","examples":["acc_eg"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this mailing list. This name is displayed in the dashboard.","examples":["Black Friday Leads"]},"recipients":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of recipients present in the mailing list. This value is updated automatically when recipients are added or removed from the mailing list.","examples":[1000]},"variables":{"type":"array","description":"An array of the dynamic fields present in the mailing list. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the dynamic field. This is the value without the curly braces. For example, if the dynamic field is `{exampleA}`, the name will be `exampleA`.","examples":["salutation","internal_id","loginURL"]}}}},"longest_address_line":{"type":"string","description":"This is the longest address line present across all recipients in the mailing list. We keep track of this to ensure the address box on postcard templates is large enough to fit the longest address.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"address_validation":{"type":"object","description":"Address validation is a value-added service that we offer to ensure your mailings are only charged for and sent to real, deliverable addresses. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","properties":{"requested":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether address validation has been requested for the mailing list.","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"completed":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether all addresses in the mailing list have been validated.","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"recipients":{"type":"object","description":"The number of recipients that have passed or failed address validation.","properties":{"passed":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of recipients that have passed address validation.","examples":[0,100],"default":0},"failed":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of recipients that have failed address validation.","examples":[0,10],"default":0}}}}},"created":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the mailing list was created. We use UNIX timestamps to avoid timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]}}},"MailingListRecipientObject":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"A globally unique identifier for the mailing list recipient.","examples":["mal_rcp_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The type of the object. Always `mailing_list_recipient`.","const":"mailing_list_recipient"},"mailing_list":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the mailing list that the recipient belongs to.","examples":["mal_eg"]},"account":{"type":"string","description":"The Intelliprint account ID that the mailing list belongs to.","examples":["acc_eg"]},"address":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The complete address line for the recipient.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country code of the address. This is an [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code](https://www.iban.com/country-codes). Example: `GB`.","examples":["GB","US","HK"],"default":"GB"}}},"variables":{"type":"object","description":"An arbitrary object of the dynamic fields for this recipient. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"salutation":"Mr.","internal_id":"12345","loginURL":"https://abc.xyz/login"}]},"address_validation_status":{"type":"string","description":"The address validation status for this recipient's address. Address validation for a recipient is only performed if address validation has been requested for the mailing list.","enum":["passed","failed","pending","not_requested"],"default":"not_requested"},"created":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) of when the mailing list recipient was created. We use UNIX timestamps to avoid timezone-based issues.","examples":[1761955200]}}}}},"paths":{"/prints":{"post":{"tags":["Prints"],"summary":"Create a print job","description":"To quickly start sending, use the `content` field to provide the text/HTML content for your mail item and provide the `recipients` you want to send your mail item to.\n\nFor advanced use cases, you can start sending pre-designed templates instead with the `template` field to `recipients` or a `mailing_list`.\n\nFor cases where you generate the entire mail item on your own, you can just provide us the `file` with pre-inserted addresses or the `file` along with `recipients` or a `mailing_list`.\n\nDownload `file` examples: [Single letter example](https://api-docs.intelliprint.net/demo_files/single_letter.pdf) or [Multi-letter example (Split by phrase \"Dear\")](https://api-docs.intelliprint.net/demo_files/multiple_letters.pdf)\n\n>[!tip] \n> Print jobs are not sent out till you set the `confirmed` parameter to `true`.","operationId":"prints.create","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/prints \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'content=Dear Mr. Doe, welcome to the Acme family!' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][name]=John Doe' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][line]=123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][postcode]=AB1 2CD' \\ \n  -d 'confirmed=false'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst print = await ip.prints.create({\n  content: `Dear Mr. Doe, welcome to the Acme family!`,\n  recipients: [\n    {\n      address: {\n        name: 'John Doe',\n        line: '123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace',\n        postcode: 'AB1 2CD'\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  confirmed: false\n})"}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","description":"The type of print job to create.","enum":["letter","postcard"],"examples":["letter"],"default":"letter"},"testmode":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to run the print job in test mode. Test mode print jobs are not charged and are not sent.","examples":[true],"default":false},"confirmed":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to confirm the print job. Once confirmed, the print job is submitted for printing and cannot be updated.","examples":[true],"default":false},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Some text or HTML content to create the print job from. If you are using a template or providing a file, this field is not required.","examples":["Dear J. Doe,\n Welcome to the Acme family!","<h1>Hello, world!</h1>","<div style='color: red;'>Hello, world!</div>"]},"template":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of a pre-designed template to use for the print job. If you are providing content or a file, this field is not required.","examples":["tmpl_eg"]},"file":{"oneOf":[{"title":"Direct file upload","type":"string","format":"binary","description":"A file to generate the print job from.\n\nYou can either provide this file directly as a binary file, as a remote URL, as a Base64 encoded data object, or as a pair of images for postcards. Please select an approach above.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, Word, RTF, JPG and PNG.","examples":["@path/to/file.pdf"]},{"title":"Base64 encoded file data","type":"object","description":"A file to generate the print job from.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, Word, RTF, JPG and PNG.","required":["content","name"],"properties":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The base64 encoded content of the file to generate the print job from.","examples":["BASE64_ENCODED_PDF"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the file to generate the print job from.","examples":["Filename.pdf"]}}},{"title":"File on a remote URL","type":"object","description":"An object with the `url` property containing the URL of the file to generate the print job from.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, Word, RTF, JPG and PNG.","required":["url"],"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"The URL of the file to generate the print job from.","examples":["https://example.com/file.pdf"]}}},{"title":"Postcard front and back images direct upload","type":"object","description":"A file to generate the print job from.\n\nEspecially for postcards, instead of one document with two pages, two separate images can be provided depicting the front and back sides of the postcards.\n\nThe accepted file formats are JPG and PNG.","required":["front_image","back_image"],"properties":{"front_image":{"type":"string","format":"binary","description":"The front image of the postcard to generate the print job from.","examples":["@path/to/front_image.jpg"]},"back_image":{"type":"string","format":"binary","description":"The back image of the postcard to generate the print job from.","examples":["@path/to/back_image.jpg"]}}},{"title":"Postcard front and back images on a remote URL","type":"object","description":"A file to generate the print job from.\n\nEspecially for postcards, instead of one document with two pages, two separate images can be provided depicting the front and back sides of the postcards.\n\nThe accepted file formats are JPG and PNG.","required":["front_image","back_image"],"properties":{"front_image":{"type":"object","description":"An object with the `url` property containing the URL of the front image of the postcard.","required":["url"],"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"The URL of the front image of the postcard to generate the print job from.\n\nThe accepted file formats are JPG and PNG.","examples":["https://example.com/front_image.jpg"]}}},"back_image":{"type":"object","description":"An object with the `url` property containing the URL of the back image of the postcard.","required":["url"],"properties":{"url":{"type":"string","format":"uri","description":"The URL of the back image of the postcard to generate the print job from.\n\nThe accepted file formats are JPG and PNG.","examples":["https://example.com/back_image.jpg"]}}}}}]},"reference":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly description for the print job. This value is displayed in the dashboard. You can use this value to search for this print job later.","examples":["My first print job"]},"mailing_list":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of a mailing list to send this print job to. One copy of your mail item will be sent to each recipient in the mailing list. If you are providing recipients instead, this field is not required.","examples":["mal_eg"]},"recipients":{"type":"array","description":"A list of recipients to send this print job to. One copy of your mail item will be sent to each recipient in the list. If you are providing a mailing list instead, this field is not required.\n\n>[!tip] \n> If you are providing a file of letters with pre-inserted addresses, you do not need to provide `recipients` as Intelliprint will automatically extract the addresses from the file. You may want to use splitting settings to split the print job into multiple letters.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"object","required":["line"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The complete address line for the recipient.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country code of the address. This is an [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code](https://www.iban.com/country-codes). Example: `GB`.","examples":["GB","US","HK"],"default":"GB"}}},"variables":{"type":"object","description":"An arbitrary object of the dynamic fields for this recipient. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"salutation":"Mr.","internal_id":"12345","loginURL":"https://abc.xyz/login"}]}}}},"splitting":{"type":"object","description":"Splitting settings for the print job. Used when a single file contains multiple letters with pre-inserted addresses. Splitting is only available for letters.","properties":{"method":{"type":"string","description":"The method to use to split the print job into mailings.","enum":["none","split_on_phrase","split_on_pages","mailing_list"],"default":"none"},"phrase":{"type":"string","description":"The phrase to search for on each page to split the print job into multiple letters. Only used when method is `split_on_phrase`. The phrase should appear once on the first page of each letter. Tip: Use white text to hide the phrase from recipients.","examples":["Dear"]},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages each letter in a split print job should have. Only used if method is `split_on_pages`.","examples":[1]}}},"printing":{"type":"object","description":"Printing settings for the print job, including quality, color, single- or double-sided printing, and finishing options.","properties":{"double_sided":{"type":"string","description":"Whether this print job should be printed on both sides of the paper.\n\nIf you choose `mixed`, you need to specify the page indexes to print double sided in the `double_sided_specific_pages` property.\n\nThis is only available for letters.","enum":["no","yes","mixed"],"default":"no"},"double_sided_specific_pages":{"type":"array","description":"The page indexes to print double-sided. Only used if `double_sided` is `mixed`. This is only available for letters. Page indexes are 0-indexed (first page is index 0).","items":{"type":"integer","description":"The page index to print double-sided.","examples":[0,1,2]}},"premium_quality":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in premium quality. Premium quality is optional for letters, while postcards are always printed in premium quality due to their glossy finish.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"black_and_white":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in black and white instead of color. This is only available for letters.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"matt_finish":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed with a matt finish. This is only available for postcards as letters are always printed on matt paper.","examples":[true,false],"default":false}}},"postage":{"type":"object","description":"Postage settings for the print job, including the postage service, ideal envelope (or postcard size), and mailing date.","properties":{"service":{"type":"string","description":"The postage service to use for the print job. Postcards can currently only be sent with `uk_second_class` or `uk_first_class` services.","enum":["uk_second_class","uk_second_class_signed_for","uk_first_class","uk_first_class_signed_for","uk_special_delivery_9am","uk_special_delivery","international","tracked_24","tracked_48"],"default":"uk_second_class"},"ideal_envelope":{"type":"string","description":"The ideal envelope size for letters or postcard size for postcards.\n\nAvailable values are `c4`, `c5`, `c4_plus`, `a4_box` for letters, and `postcard_a6`, `postcard_a5` or `postcard_a5_enveloped` for postcards. Default is `c5` for letters and `postcard_a6` for postcards.\n\nThe API may upgrade a letter to a larger envelope if the content is too large for the chosen envelope size.","enum":["c4","c5","c4_plus","a4_box","postcard_a6","postcard_a5","postcard_a5_enveloped"],"default":"c5"},"mail_date":{"type":"integer","format":"int64","description":"The mailing date for the print job. This is when we will print and ship your mailing, not when it will arrive at the recipient's address. This is a [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) (day-adjusted). Use this field to schedule mailings for a future date.","examples":[1761955200]}}},"background":{"type":"object","description":"Background settings for the print job. Specify which backgrounds to apply to different pages. This is only available for letters.","properties":{"first_page":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the first page of the print job. Typically a letterhead or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]},"other_pages":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the other pages of the print job. Typically a continuation design or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]}}},"confidential":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be considered confidential. Confidential print jobs cannot be viewed by other users in the dashboard.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"extra_documents":{"type":"array","description":"Extra documents (or additional documents) can be sent alongside letters in the print job. These can include standard terms and conditions, brochures, forms, or other supplementary materials.\n\nA copy of all extra documents is sent with each letter in the print job.\n\nThe order they appear in the array is the order they will follow during printing.\n\nAcceptable formats are PDF, RTF, and Word documents.\n\nExtra documents are only available for letters, as postcards have a fixed size.","items":{"type":"object","required":["document"],"properties":{"document":{"oneOf":[{"title":"Direct file upload","type":"string","format":"binary","description":"The extra document file to include in the print job.\n\nYou can either provide this file directly as a binary file or as a Base64 encoded data object. Please select an approach above.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","examples":["@path/to/file.pdf"]},{"title":"Base64 encoded file data","type":"object","description":"The base64 encoded extra document data to be included in the print job.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","required":["content","name"],"properties":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The Base64 encoded content of the extra document to include in the print job.","examples":["BASE64_ENCODED_PDF"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the extra document to include in the print job.","examples":["Filename.pdf"]}}}]},"apply_background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to apply the `background.other_pages` to the extra document. Default is false.","examples":[true,false],"default":false}}}},"remove_letters":{"type":"object","description":"Used alongside the `splitting` settings to remove specific letters from the print job.","properties":{"with_phrase":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"If this phrase is present in a letter, it will be removed from the print job. This is only available for letters.","examples":["EMAIL ONLY"]}}},"nudge":{"type":"object","description":"For print jobs with pre-inserted addresses, nudging helps position the address within the envelope window. Nudging is only available for letters.","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","description":"The horizontal distance to nudge the address window to the right in millimeters.","examples":[2]},"y":{"type":"number","description":"The vertical distance to nudge the address window down in millimeters.","examples":[-1]}}},"confirmation_email":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to send a confirmation email to the account owner once the print job is confirmed. By default, no confirmation email is sent.","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"address_window":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The position of the address window on the page. This is only available for letters.","enum":["left","right"],"default":"left"},"insert":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The ID of an insert to use for the print job. Inserts are a value-added service - We can keep stock of and insert any pre-printed materials provided ahead of time into envelopes for you. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","examples":["ins_eg"]},"metadata":{"type":"object","description":"This is an arbitrary object that can be used to store any additional data alongside your print job. This is not used by Intelliprint and is only for your own use.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"uploaded_by":"J. Doe","internal_id":"123456"}]}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"get":{"tags":["Prints"],"summary":"List all print jobs","description":"Returns a paginated list of all the available print jobs with optional filtering.","operationId":"prints.list","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl 'https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/prints?limit=10&skip=0' \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst list = await ip.prints.list({\n  limit: 10,\n  skip: 0\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"limit","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to return in the response.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"default":10,"examples":[1]}},{"name":"skip","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to skip (For pagination).","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":0,"examples":[0]}},{"name":"sort_field","in":"query","description":"The field to sort the print jobs by.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["created","confirmed_at","reference","type","letters","pages","sheets","letters.returned.date","cost.after_tax","cost.amount"],"default":"created"}},{"name":"sort_order","in":"query","description":"The order to sort the print jobs in.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["asc","desc"],"default":"desc"}},{"name":"fields","in":"query","description":"A filtered down list of fields to return in the response. Example: [\"id\", \"reference\", \"letters.status\"]. By default, all fields are returned.","style":"form","explode":true,"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},{"name":"testmode","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that are in test mode (`true`) or live mode (`false`). By default, only live mode print jobs are returned.","schema":{"type":"boolean","default":false}},{"name":"confirmed","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that are confirmed (`true`) or not confirmed (`false`). By default, both kinds are returned.","schema":{"type":"boolean"}},{"name":"type","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that are of this type. By default, both types are returned.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["letter","postcard"]}},{"name":"reference","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that have this exact reference (Case-sensitive)","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"letters.status","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that have at least one letter with this status. Multiple values are possible by separating them with a comma. Example: `waiting_to_print,printing`.","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"letters.returned.acknowledged","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those print jobs that have at least one letter that has been acknowledged (`true`) or not acknowledged (`false`) as returned in the dashboard. By default, both kinds are returned.","schema":{"type":"boolean"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListObject"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"}}}}]}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/prints/{id}":{"get":{"tags":["Prints"],"summary":"Retrieve a print job","description":"Retrieves a print job by ID.","operationId":"prints.retrieve","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/prints/print-job-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst print = await ip.prints.retrieve('print-job-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the print job to retrieve.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"post":{"tags":["Prints"],"summary":"Update a print job","description":"Updates a print job.","operationId":"prints.update","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/prints/print-job-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'reference=My updated print job' \\ \n  -d 'confirmed=true'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst print = await ip.prints.update('print-job-id', {\n  reference: 'My updated print job',\n  confirmed: true\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the print job to update.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"testmode":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to run the print job in test mode. Test mode print jobs are not charged and are not sent.","examples":[true],"default":false},"confirmed":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to confirm the print job. Once confirmed, the print job is submitted for printing and cannot be updated.","examples":[true],"default":false},"reference":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly description for the print job. This value is displayed in the dashboard. You can use this value to search for this print job later.","examples":["My first print job"]},"splitting":{"type":"object","description":"Splitting settings for the print job. Used when a single file contains multiple letters with pre-inserted addresses. Splitting is only available for letters.","properties":{"method":{"type":"string","description":"The method to use to split the print job into mailings.","enum":["none","split_on_phrase","split_on_pages","mailing_list"],"default":"none"},"phrase":{"type":"string","description":"The phrase to search for on each page to split the print job into multiple letters. Only used when method is `split_on_phrase`. The phrase should appear once on the first page of each letter. Tip: Use white text to hide the phrase from recipients.","examples":["Dear"]},"pages":{"type":"integer","description":"The number of pages each letter in a split print job should have. Only used if method is `split_on_pages`.","examples":[1]}}},"printing":{"type":"object","description":"Printing settings for the print job, including quality, color, single or double-sided printing, and finishing options.","properties":{"premium_quality":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in premium quality. Premium quality is optional for letters, while postcards are always printed in premium quality due to their glossy finish.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"black_and_white":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed in black and white instead of color. This is only available for letters.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"matt_finish":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be printed with a matt finish. This is only available for postcards as letters are always printed on matt paper.","examples":[true,false],"default":false}}},"postage":{"type":"object","description":"Postage settings for the print job, including the postage service, ideal envelope (or postcard size), and mailing date.","properties":{"service":{"type":"string","description":"The postage service to use for the print job. Postcards can currently only be sent with `uk_second_class` or `uk_first_class` services.","enum":["uk_second_class","uk_second_class_signed_for","uk_first_class","uk_first_class_signed_for","uk_special_delivery_9am","uk_special_delivery","international","tracked_24","tracked_48"],"default":"uk_second_class"},"ideal_envelope":{"type":"string","description":"The ideal envelope size for letters or postcard size for postcards.\n\nAvailable values are `c4`, `c5`, `c4_plus`, `a4_box` for letters, and `postcard_a6`, `postcard_a5` or `postcard_a5_enveloped` for postcards. Default is `c5` for letters and `postcard_a6` for postcards.\n\nThe API may upgrade a letter to a larger envelope if the content is too large for the chosen size.","enum":["c4","c5","c4_plus","a4_box","postcard_a6","postcard_a5","postcard_a5_enveloped"],"default":"c5"},"mail_date":{"type":"integer","description":"The mailing date for the print job. This is when we will print and ship your mailing, not when it will arrive at the recipient's address. This is a [UNIX timestamp](https://w.wiki/bUA) (day-adjusted). Use this field to schedule mailings for a future date.","examples":[1761955200]}}},"background":{"type":"object","description":"Background settings for the print job. Specify which backgrounds to apply to different pages. This is only available for letters.","properties":{"first_page":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the first page of the print job. Typically a letterhead or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]},"other_pages":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the background to apply to the other pages of the print job. Typically a continuation design or logo.","examples":["bg_eg"]}}},"confidential":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether this print job should be considered confidential. Confidential print jobs cannot be viewed by other users in the dashboard.","examples":[true,false],"default":false},"extra_documents":{"type":"array","description":"Extra documents (or additional documents) can be sent alongside letters in the print job. These can include standard terms and conditions, brochures, forms, or other supplementary materials.\n\nA copy of all extra documents is sent with each letter in the print job.\n\nThe order they appear in the array is the order they will follow during printing.\n\nAcceptable formats are PDF, RTF, and Word documents.\n\nExtra documents are only available for letters, as postcards have a fixed size.","items":{"type":"object","required":["document"],"properties":{"document":{"oneOf":[{"title":"Direct file upload","type":"string","format":"binary","description":"The extra document file to include in the print job.\n\nYou can either provide this file directly as a binary file or as a Base64 encoded data object. Please select an approach above.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","examples":["@path/to/file.pdf"]},{"title":"Base64 encoded file data","type":"object","description":"The base64 encoded extra document data to be included in the print job.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","required":["content","name"],"properties":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The Base64 encoded content of the extra document to include in the print job.","examples":["BASE64_ENCODED_PDF"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the extra document to include in the print job.","examples":["Filename.pdf"]}}}]},"apply_background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to apply the `background.other_pages` to the extra document. Default is false.","examples":[true,false],"default":false}}}},"remove_letters":{"type":"object","description":"Used alongside the `splitting` settings to remove specific letters from the print job.","properties":{"with_phrase":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"If this phrase is present in a letter, it will be removed from the print job. This is only available for letters.","examples":["EMAIL ONLY"]}}},"nudge":{"type":"object","description":"For print jobs with pre-inserted addresses, nudging helps position the address within the envelope window. Nudging is only available for letters.","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","description":"The horizontal distance to nudge the address window to the right in millimeters.","examples":[2]},"y":{"type":"number","description":"The vertical distance to nudge the address window down in millimeters.","examples":[-1]}}},"confirmation_email":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to send a confirmation email to the account owner once the print job is confirmed. By default, no confirmation email is sent.","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"address_window":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The position of the address window on the page. This is only available for letters.","enum":["left","right"],"default":"left"},"insert":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The ID of an insert to use for the print job. Inserts are a value-added service - We can keep stock of and insert any pre-printed materials provided ahead of time into envelopes for you. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","examples":["ins_eg"]},"metadata":{"type":"object","description":"This is an arbitrary object that can be used to store any additional data alongside your print job. This is not used by Intelliprint and is only for your own use.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"uploaded_by":"J. Doe","internal_id":"123456"}]}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"delete":{"tags":["Prints"],"summary":"Delete or cancel a print job","description":"This method attempts to cancel each `waiting_to_print` mail item in a `confirmed` print job.\nFor unconfirmed print jobs, it will delete the print job completely instead.\n\nYour account will be refunded for the cost of the mail items that get cancelled.\n\n> [!tip] \n> If some letters have already been sent or are in processing, those will not be cancelled or refunded.","operationId":"prints.delete","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X DELETE https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/prints/print-job-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst deleted = await ip.prints.delete('print-job-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the print job to delete.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Some (At least one) or all mail items were cancelled successfully","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PrintObject"}}}},"202":{"description":"The entire unconfirmed print job was deleted successfully","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deleted print job.","examples":["print_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `print`.","const":"print"},"deleted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the print job was successfully deleted. Always `true`.","examples":[true]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/backgrounds":{"post":{"tags":["Backgrounds"],"summary":"Create a background","description":"Store your background artwork with Intelliprint, making it easy to repeatedly use in print jobs by just referencing the ID.\n\nSpecify the Background's ID to a print job's `background.first_page` or `background.other_pages` for it to be applied.","operationId":"backgrounds.create","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/backgrounds \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -F 'file=@path/to/my/background.pdf' \\ \n  -F 'name=Company Letterhead'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\nimport {createReadStream} from 'fs'\n\nconst background = await ip.backgrounds.create({\n  file: createReadStream('path/to/my/background.pdf'),\n  name: 'Company Letterhead'\n})"}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["file"],"properties":{"file":{"oneOf":[{"title":"Direct file upload","type":"string","format":"binary","description":"The PDF or Word document to use as the background.\n\nYou can either provide this file directly as a binary file or as a Base64 encoded data object. Please select an approach above.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","examples":["@path/to/file.pdf"]},{"title":"Base64 encoded file data","type":"object","description":"The base64 encoded background file data.\n\nThe accepted file formats are PDF, RTF and Word documents.","required":["content","name"],"properties":{"content":{"type":"string","description":"The Base64 encoded content of the background file.","examples":["BASE64_ENCODED_PDF"]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the background file.","examples":["Filename.pdf"]}}}]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this background. This name is used for the selection menu in the dashboard print editor.","examples":["Company Letterhead"]},"team":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"To restrict dashboard-based usage of this background to a certain team, specify the team's ID here.","examples":[null]}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BackgroundObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"get":{"tags":["Backgrounds"],"summary":"List all backgrounds","description":"Returns a paginated list of all the available backgrounds with optional filtering.","operationId":"backgrounds.list","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl 'https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/backgrounds?limit=10&skip=0' \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst list = await ip.backgrounds.list({\n  limit: 10,\n  skip: 0\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"limit","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to return in the response.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"default":10,"examples":[1]}},{"name":"skip","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to skip (For pagination).","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":0,"examples":[0]}},{"name":"sort_field","in":"query","description":"The field to sort the backgrounds by.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["created","name"],"default":"created"}},{"name":"sort_order","in":"query","description":"The order to sort the backgrounds in.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["asc","desc"],"default":"desc"}},{"name":"fields","in":"query","description":"A filtered down list of fields to return in the response. Example: [\"id\", \"name\", \"file.name\"]. By default, all fields are returned.","style":"form","explode":true,"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},{"name":"team","in":"query","description":"Filters the results to only those backgrounds that are assigned to this team ID.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListObject"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BackgroundObject"}}}}]}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/backgrounds/{id}":{"get":{"tags":["Backgrounds"],"summary":"Retrieve a background","description":"Retrieves a background by ID.\n\nEach time a background is retrieved, the `pdf` field is updated to a new signed URL that will expire after 1 hour.","operationId":"backgrounds.retrieve","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/backgrounds/background-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst background = await ip.backgrounds.retrieve('background-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the background to retrieve.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BackgroundObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"post":{"tags":["Backgrounds"],"summary":"Update a background","description":"Updates a background.","operationId":"backgrounds.update","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/backgrounds/background-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'name=Updated Company Letterhead'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst background = await ip.backgrounds.update('background-id', {\n  name: 'Updated Company Letterhead'\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the background to update.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this background. This name is used for the selection menu in the dashboard print editor.","examples":["Company Letterhead"]},"team":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"To restrict dashboard-based usage of this background to a certain team, specify the team's ID here.","examples":[null]}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/BackgroundObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"delete":{"tags":["Backgrounds"],"summary":"Delete a background","description":"Deletes a background.\n\n> [!tip] \n> A deletion request will fail if any print job has utilized this background in the last 90 days, as we need to keep the background available for reproduction till the print job is archived, 90 days from its creation date.","operationId":"backgrounds.delete","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X DELETE https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/backgrounds/background-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst deleted = await ip.backgrounds.delete('background-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the background to delete.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deleted background.","examples":["bg_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `background`.","const":"background"},"deleted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the background was successfully deleted. Always `true`.","examples":[true]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/mailing_lists":{"post":{"tags":["Mailing Lists"],"summary":"Create a mailing list","description":"Store thousands of recipients in a single mailing list, and send mail items to all of them at once easily.\n\nYou can add recipients in bulk while creating the mailing list.","operationId":"mailing_lists.create","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'name=Black Friday Leads' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][name]=John Doe' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][line]=123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][postcode]=AB1 2CD' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][variables][salutation]=Mr.'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst mailingList = await ip.mailing_lists.create({\n  name: 'Black Friday Leads',\n  recipients: [\n    {\n      address: {\n        name: 'John Doe',\n        line: '123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace',\n        postcode: 'AB1 2CD'\n      },\n      variables: {\n        salutation: 'Mr.'\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})"}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this mailing list. This name is displayed in the dashboard.","examples":["Black Friday Leads"]},"recipients":{"type":"array","description":"An optional list of recipients to add to the mailing list.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"object","required":["line"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The complete address line for the recipient.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country code of the address. This is an [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code](https://www.iban.com/country-codes). Example: `GB`.","examples":["GB","US","HK"],"default":"GB"}}},"variables":{"type":"object","description":"An arbitrary object of the dynamic fields for this recipient. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"salutation":"Mr.","internal_id":"12345","loginURL":"https://abc.xyz/login"}]}}}},"address_validation":{"type":"object","description":"Whether to request address validation for the mailing list. This is a value-added service that we offer to ensure your mailings are only charged for and sent to real, deliverable addresses. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","properties":{"requested":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to perform address validation on all the recipients in the mailing list.","examples":[false,true],"default":false}}}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"get":{"tags":["Mailing Lists"],"summary":"List all mailing lists","description":"Returns a paginated list of all the available mailing lists.","operationId":"mailing_lists.list","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl 'https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists?limit=10&skip=0' \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst list = await ip.mailing_lists.list({\n  limit: 10,\n  skip: 0\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"limit","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to return in the response.","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"default":10,"examples":[1]}},{"name":"skip","in":"query","description":"The number of objects to skip (For pagination).","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":0,"examples":[0]}},{"name":"sort_field","in":"query","description":"The field to sort the mailing lists by.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["created","name","recipients"],"default":"created"}},{"name":"sort_order","in":"query","description":"The order to sort the mailing lists in.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["asc","desc"],"default":"desc"}},{"name":"fields","in":"query","description":"A filtered down list of fields to return in the response. Example: [\"id\", \"name\", \"recipients\"]. By default, all fields are returned.","style":"form","explode":true,"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ListObject"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListObject"}}}}]}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/mailing_lists/{id}":{"get":{"tags":["Mailing Lists"],"summary":"Retrieve a mailing list","description":"Retrieves a mailing list by ID.","operationId":"mailing_lists.retrieve","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists/mailing-list-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst mailingList = await ip.mailing_lists.retrieve('mailing-list-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the mailing list to retrieve.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"post":{"tags":["Mailing Lists"],"summary":"Update a mailing list","description":"Updates a mailing list.\n\nYou can add or replace recipients in bulk using this endpoint.","operationId":"mailing_lists.update","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists/mailing-list-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'name=Black Friday Leads' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][name]=John Doe' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][line]=123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][address][postcode]=AB1 2CD' \\ \n  -d 'recipients[0][variables][salutation]=Mr.'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst mailingList = await ip.mailing_lists.update('mailing-list-id', {\n  name: 'Black Friday Leads',\n  recipients: [\n    {\n      address: {\n        name: 'John Doe',\n        line: '123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace',\n        postcode: 'AB1 2CD'\n      },\n      variables: {\n        salutation: 'Mr.'\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the mailing list to update.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"A user-friendly name for this mailing list. This name is displayed in the dashboard.","examples":["Black Friday Leads"]},"delete_old_recipients":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to delete all the currently stored recipients from the mailing list.","examples":[false,true],"default":false},"recipients":{"type":"array","description":"An optional list of new recipients to add to the mailing list.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"object","required":["line"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The complete address line for the recipient.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country code of the address. This is an [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code](https://www.iban.com/country-codes). Example: `GB`.","examples":["GB","US","HK"],"default":"GB"}}},"variables":{"type":"object","description":"An arbitrary object of the dynamic fields for this recipient. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"salutation":"Mr.","internal_id":"12345","loginURL":"https://abc.xyz/login"}]}}}},"address_validation":{"type":"object","description":"Whether to request address validation for the mailing list. This is a value-added service that we offer to ensure your mailings are only charged for and sent to real, deliverable addresses. Please contact us at [hello@intelliprint.net](mailto:hello@intelliprint.net) to enable this service for your account.","properties":{"requested":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether to perform address validation on all the recipients in the mailing list.","examples":[false,true],"default":false}}}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"delete":{"tags":["Mailing Lists"],"summary":"Delete a mailing list","description":"Deletes a mailing list along with all the recipients in the mailing list.","operationId":"mailing_lists.delete","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X DELETE https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists/mailing-list-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst deleted = await ip.mailing_lists.delete('mailing-list-id')"}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the mailing list to delete.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","description":"The ID of the deleted mailing list.","examples":["mal_eg"]},"object":{"type":"string","description":"The object type. Always `mailing_list`.","const":"mailing_list"},"deleted":{"type":"boolean","description":"Whether the mailing list was successfully deleted. Always `true`.","examples":[true]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}}},"/mailing_lists/{mailing_list}/recipients":{"post":{"tags":["Mailing List Recipients"],"summary":"Create a mailing list recipient","description":"Creates a single new mailing list recipient.\n\n> [!note] \n> You can add or replace recipients in bulk using the [mailing lists](#tag/mailing-lists/post/mailing_lists) endpoints.","operationId":"mailing_list_recipients.create","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl -X POST https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists/mailing-list-id \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY' \\ \n  -d 'address[name]=John Doe' \\ \n  -d 'address[line]=123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace' \\ \n  -d 'address[postcode]=AB1 2CD' \\ \n  -d 'variables[salutation]=Mr.'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-here')\n\nconst recipient = await ip.mailing_list_recipients.create('mailing-list-id', {\n  address: {\n    name: 'John Doe',\n    line: '123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace',\n    postcode: 'AB1 2CD'\n  },\n  variables: {\n    salutation: 'Mr.'\n  }\n})"}],"parameters":[{"name":"mailing_list","in":"path","required":true,"description":"The ID of the mailing list the recipient belongs to.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["address"],"properties":{"address":{"type":"object","required":["line"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"The name of the recipient.","examples":["John Doe"]},"line":{"type":"string","description":"The complete address line for the recipient.","examples":["123 Main St, Anytown, Anyplace"]},"postcode":{"type":"string","description":"The postal code of the address.","examples":["AB1 2CD","90210","411057"]},"country":{"type":"string","description":"The country code of the address. This is an [ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code](https://www.iban.com/country-codes). Example: `GB`.","examples":["GB","US","HK"],"default":"GB"}}},"variables":{"type":"object","description":"An arbitrary object of the dynamic fields for this recipient. Dynamic fields are used to tailor templates uniquely for each recipient.","additionalProperties":{"x-additionalPropertiesName":"anyKeyName","x-stainless-any":true},"examples":[{"salutation":"Mr.","internal_id":"12345","loginURL":"https://abc.xyz/login"}]}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Successful response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailingListRecipientObject"}}}},"400":{"description":"Example error response","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorObject"}}}}}},"get":{"tags":["Mailing List Recipients"],"summary":"List all recipients in a mailing list","description":"Returns a list of all the available mailing list recipients with pagination.","operationId":"mailing_list_recipients.list","x-codeSamples":[{"label":"cURL","lang":"cURL","source":"curl 'https://api.intelliprint.net/v1/mailing_lists/mailing-list-id/recipients?limit=10&skip=0' \\ \n  -H 'Authorization: YOUR_API_KEY'"},{"label":"Node.js SDK","lang":"JavaScript","source":"import Intelliprint from 'intelliprint'\nconst ip = Intelliprint('your-api-key-he